# Bloatmaw — a floating mass of flesh for the FPS roster. One great ball of a
# body, mostly mouth, hovering above the floor on nothing at all: the first
# legless, floorless character in the cast.
#
# THE READ, in silhouette order: a hunched sprawling mass of wet meat that is
# no longer a sphere from any angle — a heavy jutting jaw under a maw a third
# of the body's own width, a shelving brow ridge shading two MISMATCHED ember
# eyes, ear-frills off the flanks, a ragged raked crest and a hunched back,
# and lumpy sagging folds where the flesh gathers under its own weight. The
# maw splits the whole front with its ring of irregular bone teeth and the
# ember core burning in the throat. And, absurd against all that bulk, two
# withered arms dangle off the flanks with broken shackles at the wrists. No
# legs, no ground contact — the hover gap is the character.
#
# r2 (this pass): the owner said the body "needs to have a more complex shape,
# would be good if it had things like ears or jaw or brow nose etc." The old
# ball had been a clean sphere and, worse, wore two bright pale-BLUE and GREEN
# orb eyes stuck proud of the surface like googly toys. So the eyes were
# replaced — small dim embers (burnt crimson + smoke-amber, neither blue nor
# green) seated IN sockets under a continuous brow ridge, so the silhouette
# around them is flesh, not a sphere off a sphere — and the mass was rebuilt
# with jaw, jowls, brow, nasal slits, ear-frills, a back hump and a ragged
# crown, all deliberately uneven so no yaw reads as a plain circle.
#
# FLOATING. `stance` is OMITTED on purpose (see the model block): the grammar
# knows only humanoid/digitigrade and this body has no legs at all. The maw,
# teeth, eyes and throat core are GEOMETRY (prims), not a painted decal:
# there is no reference mesh to bake, and the painted-face road has failed
# this project repeatedly (face.ts's header records four rebuilds). No sheet
# block, so the registry wears ZOMBIE_FLAT.
#
# THE MAW IS NOT A CARVE. A carve into a body this big is painted by the BALL,
# not by whatever sits in the cavity: the paint rule is arg-min of the
# primitive's signed distance, and a point on a carved wall is DEEP inside the
# ball, so the ball always wins the pixel and a dark or glowing throat prim
# inside the hole would render as plain flesh. So the maw is an additive dark
# mass that owns its own surface by protruding from the ball's front, with the
# lit core protruding further still. (Cyclops paid for the carve version: two
# carve attempts left GPU holes the CPU field did not have, 2026-08-22.)
model bloatmaw
  # height = the TOP OF THE BALL, not a standing crown. The whole body hovers:
  # ball centre y = 1.08, y-semi-axis 0.749 -> top 1.829, underside 0.302.
  # THE HOVER GAP IS 0.302 m. Move HOVER (the centre height) and re-check the
  # top against this number if the body is ever rescaled. The r2 crest/ears
  # all sit under the ball's own top (tallest crest tip y 1.81), so height is
  # still the ball's. Nothing in the format enforces ground contact — there is
  # no sole-at-y=0 rule in blob-checks.ts or validate.ts — which is exactly
  # why a floating body validates cleanly at all.
  height 1.83
  # NO `stance` LINE. `checkStance` is the format's one intent check and it
  # only knows humanoid/digitigrade knees; omitting the line means "not
  # checked", which is the honest state for a body with no leg chain. A
  # defaulted intent would be a guess.

skeleton
  # THE ROOT IS THE BALL'S CENTRE, not a pelvis. `root pelvis at 1.08` puts
  # the root bone's HEAD at the hover centre; the 0.06 length is a stub up to
  # 1.14 so children hang off its tail per the grammar. The name `pelvis` is
  # inherited from the format and is a lie here — read it as "ball centre".
  root pelvis at 1.08 len=0.06

  # A vertical axis through the ball: it exists for the gait wiring (the
  # motion profile maps spine/neck/skull by name) and to hang the crown spurs
  # on. The flesh ignores it.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up len=0.30          # 1.14 -> 1.44
  bone neck  parent=spine  dir=up len=0.16          # 1.44 -> 1.60
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up len=0.14          # 1.60 -> 1.74

  # THE MAW AXIS — forward out of the ball centre to its front surface. Every
  # mouth prim (dark maw, teeth, lit core) rides this bone with an `offset=`,
  # so the whole face moves as one if the ball is rescaled.
  bone maw parent=pelvis dir=fwd len=0.70           # 1.14 -> z 0.70

  mirror
    # TINY ARMS. The clavicle does NOT run sideways: it runs DOWN-OUT at 63
    # degrees so the shoulder seats near the ball's EQUATOR, where the surface
    # is at x 0.62 — an arm rooted higher or lower sits deep inside a sphere
    # that has barely curved in, and gets no daylight (the goblin lesson: the
    # lever on arm clearance is the BODY's width, not the arm's).
    # Shoulder lands at (0.633, 1.118); the ball surface there is x 0.618, so
    # the 0.085 shoulder ball is welded in by ~7 cm and pokes out by ~10 cm.
    bone clavicle parent=spine    dir=down tilt=63 len=0.71
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=60 len=0.13
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down tilt=50 pitch=8 len=0.11
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down tilt=45 pitch=10 len=0.07
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # THE BALL — one great hanging meat balloon. Three blended masses: the
  # main ellipsoid carries the silhouette, the other two fatten the crown
  # and the underside so it reads as a sagging organ rather than a pool
  # ball. `core` marks the main mass for the fuse probe.
  # ============================================================
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 r=0.720 wide=0.86 tall=1.04 deep=1.00 blend=0.030 core
  # Upper swell: the balloon's shoulders, x-semi 0.60 at y 1.17.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.10 r=0.600 wide=0.86 tall=0.92 deep=0.92 blend=0.045
  # Lower sag: the heavy underside, dropped 0.30 and squashed tall. This is
  # what sets the 0.302 hover gap.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0,-0.30,0) r=0.520 wide=0.86 tall=0.92 deep=0.90 blend=0.045
  # FLESHY IRREGULARITY: three off-centre swells that poke a couple of
  # centimetres proud of the ball, so the silhouette is a sagging organ rather
  # than a perfect sphere (a perfect sphere reads as a prop). Blends are loose
  # (0.04) so they merge into the mass instead of reading as separate lumps.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.42 offset=(0.34,0.06,0.14) r=0.170 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 deep=1.15 blend=0.040
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(-0.36,-0.16,0.10) r=0.160 wide=1.10 tall=1.00 deep=1.10 blend=0.040
  blob torso on spine  at=0.15 offset=(0.05,0.10,-0.34) r=0.180 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=1.00 blend=0.045

  # ============================================================
  # THE MAW — the whole front of the ball. A wide dark mass bulging ~5 cm
  # proud of the ball's front so it OWNS its pixels (see the header: a carved
  # cavity would belong to the ball). Footprint 1.00 m wide x 0.65 m tall on
  # a ball 1.24 m wide — a third of the body. color 180406 is near-black
  # blood: the deepColor of a mouth, not a paint region.
  # ============================================================
  blob head on maw at=0.92 offset=(0,-0.09,0) r=0.44 wide=1.14 tall=0.74 deep=0.22 blend=0.012 color=180406
  # A dull ember haze in the throat, just proud of the maw so it owns a ring.
  blob head on maw at=0.94 offset=(0,-0.09,0.05) r=0.24 wide=1.15 tall=0.85 deep=0.55 blend=0.030 color=7a1404 glow=0.35
  # THE LIT CORE: a burning ember in the middle of the maw, protruding ~7 cm
  # past the dark mass so it is the outermost prim there and can glow. One
  # strong light on the character; the colour IS the emission (glow rides the
  # prim's own colour, per the grammar).
  blob head on maw at=0.94 offset=(0,-0.09,0.07) r=0.15 wide=1.05 tall=0.95 deep=1.00 blend=0.020 color=ff5a10 glow=0.95

  # ---- TEETH — irregular, none repeated -------------------------------
  # Upper row: five fangs hanging off the top lip. Bases sit on the dark
  # maw's own rim (z 0.62 is inside the maw lens at these x/y), tips point
  # down-forward so they cross the dark mass and read against it. Sizes and
  # angles deliberately uneven: 0.048/0.060/0.055/0.056/0.045.
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.28,0.20,0.00) r=0.048 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.03,-0.26,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.14,0.25,0.00) r=0.060 r2=0.009 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.02,-0.30,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.00,0.27,0.00) r=0.055 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,-0.32,0.23) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.15,0.25,0.00) r=0.056 r2=0.009 blend=0.005 tip=(0.02,-0.29,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.29,0.19,0.00) r=0.045 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.03,-0.25,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  # Lower row: four chunky stubs jutting up from the bottom lip.
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.26,-0.30,0.00) r=0.050 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.02,0.24,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(-0.09,-0.34,0.00) r=0.058 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,0.27,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.10,-0.33,0.00) r=0.048 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(0.00,0.25,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55
  blob head on maw at=0.86 offset=(0.27,-0.29,0.00) r=0.054 r2=0.008 blend=0.005 tip=(-0.02,0.23,0.22) color=d8cdae gloss=0.55

  # ---- EYES — SEATED IN THE FLESH, NOT STUCK ON -----------------------
  # Two VERY uneven eyes, and this time they sit IN the ball. The old ones
  # were bright saturated spheres (pale BLUE and sick GREEN) pinned proud of
  # a smooth sphere and bulging ~0.16 m off it — googly toy eyes on a toy
  # ball, the worst thing in the frame. These are small dim embers tucked
  # into sockets under a heavy brow: the ball's OWN flesh — a shelving brow
  # above, a jowl below, an overhanging lid — carries the SILHOUETTE, while
  # the eye only fills the gap between them. From the side the outline is
  # brow and jowl, never a clean sphere off a clean sphere.
  # COLOUR: the throat core is a HOT orange ember, so the eyes are
  # deliberately NOT orange and NOT bright — one burnt ember, one dull
  # smoke-amber, both dim and desaturated so nothing reads as plastic or
  # glass. Asymmetry stays: different sizes, different heights, one
  # half-lidded by a flesh lid.
  # The brow is one continuous shelf (a single mass whose own bulges do the
  # shading) — `wide` 2.4 lets it span the whole eye line instead of sitting
  # as a separate blob over each eye. It shelves OVER the sockets, but is
  # raised high enough (offset y 0.50 -> y ~1.64) that it shades them from
  # the top third rather than swallowing them; the eyes read below it.
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(-0.02,0.50,0.06) r=0.140 wide=2.20 tall=0.46 deep=0.90 blend=0.012   # brow ridge, spans both sockets
  # Right eye (character's right, +x), the big one, set HIGH and out a touch.
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.22,0.40,-0.02) r=0.080 wide=1.05 tall=1.05 deep=0.85 blend=0.008   # socket crater (flesh, sets eye in)
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.22,0.40,0.05) r=0.060 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=0.88 blend=0.006 color=7a1c08 glow=0.70
  # A lower-lid jowl under the big eye that rises over its bottom quarter.
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.24,0.31,0.02) r=0.072 wide=1.30 tall=0.55 deep=0.90 blend=0.008
  # Left eye (character's left, -x), smaller, LOWER and more sunken: a dimmer
  # smoke-amber, half-hidden under a heavy lid. The two never read the same.
  blob head on maw at=0.78 offset=(-0.30,0.30,-0.03) r=0.066 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=0.85 blend=0.008  # socket crater
  blob head on maw at=0.78 offset=(-0.30,0.30,0.03) r=0.044 wide=1.00 tall=0.86 deep=0.84 blend=0.005 color=7a5c14 glow=0.48
  blob head on maw at=0.78 offset=(-0.30,0.36,0.04) r=0.058 wide=1.25 tall=0.50 deep=0.95 blend=0.008   # heavy lid over the small eye

  # ============================================================
  # ANATOMY — the ball stops being a sphere. All of this is the owner's
  # "ears or jaw or brow nose" brief: the mass is broken up into features
  # with their OWN outline, so no yaw reads as a plain circle. Every piece
  # is deliberately OFF-CENTRE and uneven — the asymmetry is the point, and
  # a few of them are painted so the eye can find them against the flesh.
  # ============================================================

  # ---- JAW — a real mandible under the maw, not a hole cut in the ball --
  # The maw already carries the mouth. Under it sits a heavy jutting jaw: a
  # broad flat-scaled mass that drops below the mouth line and thrusts
  # forward, so from the side the lower face is a jaw, not the ball's arc.
  # It leans a touch to +x so the whole face is not bilaterally symmetric.
  blob head on maw at=0.34 offset=(0.06,-0.30,0.16) r=0.230 wide=1.25 tall=0.78 deep=0.95 blend=0.022
  # Jowl slabs hanging off each cheek, uneven (the +x one is heavier and
  # lower), so the front silhouette has sagging cheeks either side of the jaw.
  blob head on maw at=0.40 offset=(0.40,-0.26,0.10) r=0.130 wide=1.15 tall=0.95 deep=0.95 blend=0.030
  blob head on maw at=0.36 offset=(-0.34,-0.22,0.12) r=0.105 wide=1.05 tall=0.90 deep=0.90 blend=0.030
  # A second heavy jowl lower on the +x cheek so the sag is not one smooth arc.
  blob head on maw at=0.30 offset=(0.30,-0.40,0.06) r=0.085 wide=1.10 tall=0.80 deep=0.85 blend=0.030

  # ---- NOSE / NASAL SLITS — above the maw, between the sockets ---------
  # A broad flat nose-bridge mass sitting over the maw's top lip, with two
  # dark naris slits. It breaks the smooth front between brow and maw.
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.02,0.05,0.10) r=0.090 wide=1.30 tall=0.70 deep=0.60 blend=0.012
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(0.06,0.05,0.10) r=0.050 wide=0.60 tall=0.85 deep=0.60 blend=0.008 color=12030a
  blob head on maw at=0.80 offset=(-0.03,0.05,0.10) r=0.045 wide=0.60 tall=0.85 deep=0.60 blend=0.008 color=12030a

  # ---- EARS / EAR-FRILLS — off the flanks, raked back, uneven ----------
  # Fat fleshy flaps on the upper flanks. One is a broad rounded lobe, the
  # other a thinner pointed frill — never a matching pair. They poke the
  # silhouette outward at the sides AND (raked back) backward, which is what
  # takes the side and back views off the plain-circle path. Color 6b5a44 is
  # the same horn-flesh as the crown spurs.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.40,-0.06,-0.12) r=0.110 wide=0.85 tall=1.10 deep=0.90 blend=0.030 chamfer tip=(0.10,-0.02,-0.24) color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.28 offset=(-0.38,-0.08,-0.16) r=0.070 wide=0.70 tall=1.05 deep=0.85 blend=0.028 chamfer tip=(-0.06,-0.01,-0.30) color=6b5a44
  # A small secondary nub on the +x ear so it is not one clean disc either.
  blob head on skull at=0.36 offset=(0.40,-0.10,-0.20) r=0.044 wide=0.75 tall=1.00 deep=0.80 blend=0.026 chamfer tip=(0.09,-0.05,-0.18) color=6b5a44

  # ---- BACK HANG — the rear is not smooth ------------------------------
  # A heavy hunched mass on the back, pushed to -z and off to +x, so from
  # the side the back is a hunched shoulder and from the back the outline is
  # lopsided. Then small ragged crest-frills tumbling down the spine line.
  blob head on skull at=0.20 offset=(0.18,-0.02,-0.42) r=0.200 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=1.05 blend=0.030
  blob head on skull at=0.34 offset=(0.10,-0.08,-0.30) r=0.120 wide=1.00 tall=0.95 deep=1.00 blend=0.030
  blob head on skull at=0.06 offset=(-0.14,-0.06,-0.44) r=0.140 wide=1.00 tall=0.95 deep=1.00 blend=0.030

  # ---- CROWN CREST — a bigger, uneven raked crest in place of tiny SPURS
  # The old three-pair spurs were barely a bump. This is a handful of large
  # pointed spikes raked back and to one side, each a different size, so the
  # top of the ball is a ragged crown rather than a smooth dome. Tallest tip
  # stays under the declared 1.829 ball top (the base is the skull bone at
  # y 1.60; offsets keep every tip below ~1.80). Chamfer tips make them read
  # as points, not little lollipops.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.10,-0.02,-0.06) r=0.045 r2=0.005 blend=0.006 chamfer tip=(0.06,-0.02,-0.34) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.28,-0.06,-0.02) r=0.058 r2=0.006 blend=0.006 chamfer tip=(0.14,-0.04,-0.30) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.70 offset=(0.16,-0.04,-0.10) r=0.036 r2=0.004 blend=0.006 chamfer tip=(0.07,-0.04,-0.24) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.20 offset=(-0.20,-0.06,-0.02) r=0.055 r2=0.005 blend=0.006 chamfer tip=(-0.12,-0.04,-0.30) both color=6b5a44
  blob head on skull at=0.62 offset=(0.36,-0.08,0.04) r=0.050 r2=0.005 blend=0.006 chamfer tip=(0.15,-0.06,-0.14) both color=6b5a44

  # ---- LUMPS / SAGS — the flesh gathers under its own weight ------------
  # Asymmetric boils and folds on the flanks and underbelly, each a slightly
  # different scale and pushed a little sideways, so the mid-body is never a
  # cylinder. One sits proud enough to break the outline on the heavy side.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0.40,-0.06,0.24) r=0.170 wide=1.00 tall=1.10 deep=1.05 blend=0.035
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(-0.40,-0.02,0.08) r=0.145 wide=1.00 tall=1.05 deep=1.00 blend=0.035
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0.28,-0.42,0.02) r=0.140 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.035   # heavy-side underbelly fold
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(-0.34,-0.34,-0.06) r=0.120 wide=1.00 tall=0.92 deep=1.00 blend=0.035
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0.06,-0.50,-0.02) r=0.110 wide=1.00 tall=0.85 deep=1.00 blend=0.035
  # A couple of DARK boils so the lumps read against the flesh, not as shadow.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(0.44,0.12,-0.02) r=0.085 wide=0.95 tall=1.05 deep=0.95 blend=0.020 color=2a0a06
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.00 offset=(-0.40,0.30,-0.10) r=0.075 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=1.00 blend=0.020 color=2a0a06

  # ============================================================
  # THE ARMS — withered, too weak to matter, ending in little grasping
  # hands. One mass per segment plus a palm and two fingers.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.085 blend=0.014 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.048 r2=0.036 blend=0.010 mirror
  blob arm on upperArm at=1.00 r=0.044 blend=0.010 mirror
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.038 r2=0.028 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Palm: a small flat mitt, widened across x.
  blob arm on hand at=0.55 r=0.044 wide=1.15 tall=0.85 deep=1.15 blend=0.008 mirror
  # Two crooked fingers, splayed by their own x offsets (under mirror the .r
  # copy reflects offset.x, so each hand gets a two-finger fan).
  bar arm on hand from=0.80 to=1.18 r=0.015 r2=0.005 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(0.028,0.010,0.018) tip=(0.010,-0.046,0.038) mirror
  bar arm on hand from=0.78 to=1.10 r=0.013 r2=0.004 blend=0.004 chamfer offset=(-0.024,0.004,0.010) tip=(-0.008,-0.040,0.030) mirror

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB. The ball is the head, so the parameterised
# skull ellipsoid would sit a zombie head inside it; headRadius 0.001 kills
# it and the brow/nose gates (0) emit nothing. Same idiom as gargoyle.blob.
# No `sheet` block: there is no reference mesh to bake and no hand-authored
# decal is shipped, so the registry wears ZOMBIE_FLAT.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006
  headRise   0
  headLead   0

# Diseased wet flesh: a dark raw-meat base that the shader sRGB-encodes much
# lighter than these numbers read, a red wound interior, and a bile-yellow
# mottle that differs in HUE from the base (a same-hue darker mottle is
# invisible). Wetness high — this thing is slimy — with a soft sheen rather
# than a hard specular.
palette
  baseColor     0.30 0.15 0.12
  deepColor     0.55 0.09 0.07
  charColor     0.07 0.05 0.04
  specIntensity 0.50
  specRoughness 0.34
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.16
  wetness       0.60
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.06
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.50
  mottleScale   2.4
  mottleColor   0.24 0.26 0.09
